# Keep the repository's line endings LF, whatever platform checks it out.
#
# This tree travelled through Windows/exFAT once and came back with CRLF in 263
# tracked text files: `git status` listed every one of them as rewritten (375883
# insertions and the same number of deletions) while `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol`
# showed no content change at all. `text=auto` leaves the blobs as they already
# are (LF) and `eol=lf` keeps a Windows checkout from reintroducing that churn,
# so a diff means a change again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalise opaque payloads: treating them as text would rewrite real bytes.
*.bin -text
*.dfu -text
*.pcap -text
*.webm -text

# Ghidra owns this directory, including the CRLF in `projectState`.
firmwares/*/ghidra_*.rep/** -text
